    ],
    "notes": [
     {
      "label": "Label Text",
      "content": "Among many African peoples, pipe smoking is considered an important social activity, with men in particular using long pipes that require their full attention. The ceramic bowl of this pipe, with its black burnished slip finish, resembles the local ceramic vessels."
     },
     {
      "label": "Description",
      "content": "Pipe composed of a greyish black globular ceramic bowl and a long red-brown wood stem. The exterior of the bowl is a black burnished slip, and a band of herringbone pattern is incised below the rim."
