       "extDescrAccessibility": "A ruby mineral specimen, (NMNH 17716), from the Mogok region of Burma. This is an unusual mineral specimen because it is made up of small, tabular, translucent crystals ranging from 1.5 centimeters to 1 millimeter in dimeter. The base of the ruby is an almost beige looking quartz, with red crystals fanning upward. This photo has a black to dark red background."
